{
  "$comment": [
    "Mente OS — hook wiring for Claude Code.",
    "",
    "⚠️ THIS FILE IS A STARTING POINT, NOT A FINISHED CONFIGURATION.",
    "It wires the engine's gates so they actually fire. Everything here uses",
    "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR so it works on any machine — never a home path.",
    "",
    "⭐ IF YOU ALREADY HAVE A .claude/settings.json, DO NOT REPLACE IT.",
    "Merge the 'hooks' block below into yours. Claude Code combines settings",
    "across levels, but two files at the SAME level do not merge — the one that",
    "wins silently drops the other's rules.",
    "",
    "⛔ EVERY PreToolUse GROUP NEEDS ITS 'matcher'. Without one, the hook fires",
    "on every single tool call: a narrow gate becomes a system-wide stop, and the",
    "first thing anyone does with an unusable guard is switch it off.",
    "",
    "The scripts referenced here live in Mente/hooks/ and Mente/bin/. Until they",
    "exist, these entries are inert — a missing hook script is skipped, it does",
    "not break the session."
  ],

  "hooks": {
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "bash \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/Mente/hooks/session-start.sh\"",
            "$comment": "health + structure. ⛔ Must NEVER block the session: it reports and exits 0."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],

    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Edit|Write|MultiEdit",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python3 \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/Mente/hooks/pre-edit-standards.py\"",
            "$comment": "injects the owning block's required standards before an edit. Informs, never blocks."
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python3 \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/Mente/hooks/gate-no-block.py\"",
            "$comment": "🔴 BLOCKS (exit 2): work with no block open. Measured 2026-09-06 — a full run built and published real work while `bin/status` said no block was open, because reporting it was all anything did. Ways out: MENTE_SCRATCH=1, or a file inside Mente/."
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python3 \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/Mente/hooks/gate-critical.py\"",
            "$comment": "🔴 BLOCKS (exit 2): destructive change with no rollback · closing an insufficient block."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python3 \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/Mente/hooks/gate-critical.py\"",
            "$comment": "the same gate on the command path — an edit is not the only way to do damage."
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python3 \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/Mente/hooks/gate-accounts.py\"",
            "$comment": "layer 1 of the accounts gate: reads the command TEXT. Layer 2 is .git/hooks/pre-push, which cannot be walked around."
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python3 \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/Mente/hooks/watch-external.py\"",
            "$comment": "looks before an action a stale view would invalidate — the only instant the warning is worth anything."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Agent|Task",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python3 \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/Mente/hooks/gate-handoff.py\"",
            "$comment": "a specialist that can WRITE does not launch without a declared scope."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Read|Edit|Write",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python3 \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/Mente/hooks/gate-secrets.py\"",
            "$comment": "reading secrets/ asks; writing there ALWAYS asks. Every access is logged."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },

  "permissions": {
    "$allow_comment": [
      "⭐ THE ENGINE'S OWN COMMANDS, pre-approved. 🔴 Measured 2026-09-06: a run",
      "was stopped by a permission prompt on `bin/init` and answered `open",
      "PowerShell and paste this command` — the person was exactly as unable as",
      "before, and now believed the errand was theirs.",
      "",
      "⚠️ These are READ-and-REPORT commands plus the installer. They write only",
      "inside this folder, make no network call, and every one of them is listed",
      "in Mente/CAPABILITIES.md with what it refuses to do.",
      "⛔ Nothing here grants a general shell: `git`, `rm` and anything else stay",
      "as they were."
    ],
    "allow": [
      "Bash(python3 Mente/bin/status:*)",
      "Bash(python3 Mente/bin/off:*)",
      "Bash(python3 Mente/bin/on:*)",
      "Bash(python3 Mente/bin/init:*)",
      "Bash(python3 Mente/bin/check-health:*)",
      "Bash(python3 Mente/bin/new-block:*)",
      "Bash(python3 Mente/bin/new-campaign:*)",
      "Bash(python3 Mente/bin/grade-block:*)",
      "Bash(python3 Mente/bin/generate-metrics:*)",
      "Bash(python3 Mente/bin/probes/run-all.py:*)"
    ],
    "$comment": [
      "⬜ DECLARE YOUR OWN GATES HERE — the trees the AI must not read.",
      "They must match 'gates:' in Mente/mente.config.yml: if the two disagree,",
      "⭐ THIS FILE is what actually happens and the config is only a claim.",
      "",
      "Copy this shape for each one (delete the example, it is not a real path):",
      "  \"deny\": [\"Read(~/another-project/**)\", \"Edit(~/another-project/**)\"]"
    ],
    "deny": [],
    "ask": []
  }
}
